{{proto|Germanic|tanþs|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|h₁dont-|tooth|lang=ang}}. Cognates with Old Frisian {{term|toth|tōth}}, Old Saxon {{term|tand}} (Dutch {{term|tand}}), Old High German {{term|zan}}, {{term|zand}} (German {{term|Zahn}}), Old Norse {{term|tǫnn}} (Swedish {{term|tand}}), Gothic {{term|𐍄𐌿𐌽𐌸𐌿𐍃|sc=Goth}}; and with Sanskrit {{term|दन्त|sc=Deva}} (Hindi {{term|दांत़|sc=Deva}}), Ancient Greek {{term|ὀδών|sc=polytonic}}, Latin {{term|dens}} (French {{term|dent|lang=fr}}), Old Irish {{term|dét}}, Lithuanian {{term|dantis|dantìs}}.

